# .gitignore — the list of things git is told to pretend it cannot see.
# Anything matching a line below is left out of every commit. See curriculum/15-git.md.
# This folder is plain markdown, so the list is short: junk the operating system and
# the editors leave behind, and nothing else.

# Operating system clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor and tool directories
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Deliberately NOT ignored: progress/
#
# progress/LEARNER.md, MASTERY.md, DECISIONS.md, SKILLS-BUILT.md, REVIEWS.md and
# SESSION-LOG.md are the whole point of keeping this folder in git. They are your record
# of what you learned, what you decided, and what you built — the part that is yours and
# cannot be downloaded again. Tracking them is what gives you a history you can read back.
#
# If you copy this file into a folder of your own, check you have not ignored your own
# equivalent by accident. Notes and working files look like clutter to a rule written in a
# hurry, and an ignored file is one git will never warn you about losing.
